  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-jiey-browser",
      "text": "DeepSeek Harness plugin that gives the agent **real Jiey Browser** tools over MCP.\n\n> Let DeepSeek Harness go online — one plugin, powered by Jiey.\n\nDSH is in developer preview; this plugin targets the Cordis / `tools` + `systemPrompt` surface and may need updates as DSH breaks APIs."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why Jiey (not Playwright)",
      "text": "| | Playwright plugins | **dsh-jiey-browser** |\n|---|---|---|\n| Runtime | Headless / automation profile | Real Jiey Chromium (user browser) |\n| Install funnel | `npx playwright install` | Missing Jiey → download guide |\n| Cookies / login | Separate profile | **Default off**; opt-in to reuse sessions |\n| Cleanup | Controller close | Cordis `dispose` closes owned tabs |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Requires Node.js `^22.19 || >=24` and a DSH profile.\n\n```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "from npm (public)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-jiey-browser"
    },
    {
      "section": "or",
      "text": "npm install dsh-jiey-browser\n```\n\nFrom a local checkout after `npm run build`:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add /absolute/path/to/packages/dsh-jiey-browser\n```\n\nSource: https://github.com/jiewaigongxing/dsh-jiey-browser  \nnpm: https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-jiey-browser  \nTopics: `dsh-plugin`, `deepseek-harness`, `dsh`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Prerequisites",
      "text": "Full guide: [Use with DeepSeek Harness](https://docs.browser.gongxingglobal.com/features/use-with-deepseek-harness)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Prerequisites",
      "text": "1. Install and open **Jiey Browser** so its MCP server is up (default `http://127.0.0.1:9100`).\n   - **Download only from the official site:** https://www.gongxingglobal.com/browser  \n     (macOS / Windows / Linux installers are listed there — this repo does not ship CDN links.)\n2. Discovery order: plugin `serverUrl` → `BROWSEROS_URL` / `JIEY_URL` → `~/.browseros/server.json` → `http://127.0.0.1:9100`.\n3. Health check: `GET /system/health` must return `{ status: \"ok\" }`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Prerequisites",
      "text": "If Jiey is offline, tools fail with a link to the official download page (default `https://www.gongxingglobal.com/browser`) instead of silently falling back to another browser."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configure",
      "text": "In the profile `cordis.patch.yml` (or DSH settings UI):\n\n```yaml\n- id: jiey-browser\n  config:\n    serverUrl: \"\"              # empty = auto-discover\n    scopeId: dsh-jiey-browser  # tab isolation header\n\n**Security:** `allowCookies` defaults to **false**. Turn it on only when the user explicitly wants the agent to use existing logged-in sites."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "| Tool | Maps to Jiey MCP | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `browser_open` | `tabs` new + `snapshot` | Open |\n| `browser_navigate` | `navigate` | Navigate |\n| `browser_snapshot` | `snapshot` | Refs for act |\n| `browser_read` | `read` | Markdown / text scrape |\n| `browser_act` | `act` | click / fill / press / … |\n| `browser_screenshot` | `screenshot` | Inline image (no temp file) |\n| `browser_tabs` | `tabs` list/close | List / dispose |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Local smoke (no DSH)",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run build\nnpm run smoke\n```\n\nWith Jiey running, smoke opens `https://example.com`, snapshots, and closes the tab."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
